    <GaugingStation location="Writtle" name="Wid" number="37007">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">'Essex' profile gauging a rural catchment on London Clay, flows significantly increased by STW effluent especially in summer.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Rated spillway starts at 1.25m. Full range, modular station. Weir began to subside in 1991. Flow during summer months consists predominantly of STW discharge, of which approximately 0.08 cumecs is derived from outside the catchment, adjustments needed for this. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">'Essex' profile (modified Flat V Crump) weir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Responsive catchment. Runoff increased by STW effluent returns with net import, which significantly affects flows especially in summer. Runoff reduced by industrial/agricultural abstraction.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Low-lying catchment on London Clay with scattered areas of Boulder Clay cover. Mainly rural, mixed arable and grassland, with significant urban component.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged beyond AMAX3. Allowance made for additional flow over spillway." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
